_decisions_06c71692_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"At each of two locations $i$, a warehouse ($W_i=1$) may be built only if a factory is built there ($F_i=1$); all are binary. Why not just impose $W_1+W_2\\le F_1+F_2$?","options":["It forbids building two factories when there is one warehouse","It allows a warehouse at one site and the factory at the other","It is nonlinear, while the per-location version is linear","It allows a warehouse at a place where no factory exists at all"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9430db638feab31f9f8954a7","time_limit":35,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"}]}}